flowchart TB
  accTitle: Five Steps to Configure Remote Python Debugging
  accDescr: Install debugpy on the server, configure local SSH port forwarding and connect, then start a debug process waiting for the client. Configure the editor's attach connection and path mappings, set a breakpoint, and press F5 to connect and inspect execution.
  install["1 · Install on the server<br/>pip install debugpy"]
  ssh["2 · Configure the local SSH tunnel<br/>Add to ~/.ssh/config<br/>LocalForward 5678 localhost:5678"]
  start["3 · Start the server debug process<br/>python -m debugpy<br/>--listen 0.0.0.0:5678<br/>--wait-for-client train.py"]
  config["4 · Configure .vscode/launch.json<br/>type: debugpy · request: attach<br/>connect: localhost:5678<br/>Check localRoot and remoteRoot"]
  attach["5 · Set a breakpoint and connect<br/>F5 → Python: Remote Attach"]
  install --> ssh --> start --> config --> attach
  subgraph inspection["When execution pauses"]
    direction LR
    variables["Inspect variable values<br/>View the call stack"]
    stepping["F10 · Step over<br/>F11 · Step into"]
    variables ~~~ stepping
  end
  attach --> inspection
